==Strategy==
This stage, while simple on the surface, has several ways to be taken on. The biggest challenges of Leadfoot Drive are keeping the Le'noirs at bay and not allowing the enemies to stack up. Due to the immense tankiness of the St. Pigges, who are buffed by an immense amount, it can be very difficult to gain cash and ground before the first Le'noir and Chickful A appear, therefore, a lot of the fighting will happen closer to your end of the stage.

Most of the enemies in this stage can be easily countered when on their own, but become harder to neutralize when supported. The first Owlbrow, due to the lack of enemies to back it up, can be quickly rushed by [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], which will earn you a quick burst of starting cash. The St. Pigges are best taken out by [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], but using him becomes complicated once Le'noir and Chickful A appear. The other enemies, however, aren't as easy to kill. You will have to rely on [[Long Distance]] units or [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|wavers]] to remove them.

An alternative strategy for this stage is to abuse the standing range of Le'noir and Chickful A, as well as abuse the St. Pigges' huge health pools and use [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Major Leaguer Cat]]. For a fairly cheap cost, you can safely stack a lot of them on the St. Pigges and the effective Long Distance range of Major Leaguer Cat can be used to hit the Chickful As and Le'noirs that are behind the St. Pigges, who can be easily stalled due to their relatively low damage. Once both Chickful As have died, you can finish off the St. Pigges and fight the Le'noirs with whatever you like, preferably using [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]'s [[Knockback|knockback]] to regain ground.

It's also recommended to use four meatshields on this stage, as well as units such as the aforementioned Ururun Cat and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] (or [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] who can replace them such as [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Radiant Aphrodite]]) who can hit the Le'noirs and Chickful A from a safe distance.

Ultimately, knowing how to remove each threat from the stage will be what leads you to victory.

